# ==============================================================================
# Trace — .gitignore
#
# Canonical ignore set for an Unreal Engine 5 C++ project.
#
# GOLDEN RULE: Config/ and Source/ are ALWAYS tracked. If you ever find yourself
# adding a pattern that swallows either of them, you have made a mistake — the
# project is unbuildable for everyone else without those two directories.
#
# Content/ is also tracked (binary assets go through Git LFS — see .gitattributes).
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unreal Engine generated directories
# These are recreated by UnrealBuildTool / the editor on demand. Never commit them.
# The patterns are unanchored on purpose so they also catch Plugins/*/Binaries etc.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Platforms/*/Binaries/
Platforms/*/Intermediate/

# UBT / UAT build artifacts.
# NOTE: Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. If you
# later add packaging resources that MUST be versioned (Build/Mac/Resources,
# Build/Windows/Application.ico, entitlements, ...), do not add a "!" line here —
# change this to `Build/*` and add `!Build/Mac/` style negations instead.
Build/

# Cooked/staged output and packaged builds
Packaged/
Cooked/
Archive/
*.pak
*.utoc
*.ucas

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated IDE project files
# `GenerateProjectFiles` (or Scripts/build.sh --projectfiles) recreates these.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
*.sln
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.code-workspace
Makefile
CMakeLists.txt
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
compile_commands.json
.cache/
.clangd/
.ccls-cache/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiler / linker intermediates that can escape Binaries/ and Intermediate/
# (e.g. a ThirdParty build dropped in place). Deliberately NOT listing *.dll /
# *.dylib / *.so / *.pdb here — real shipped ThirdParty libraries under
# Source/ThirdParty are legitimately versioned and are LFS-tracked instead.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.obj
*.slo
*.lo
*.gch
*.ilk
*.exp
*.idb
*.ipdb
*.iobj
*.tlog
*.d
*.dSYM/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, crash dumps, local scratch
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.stackdump
crash-*.dmp
CrashReportClient/

# Local engine-path override consumed by Scripts/_trace_common.sh.
# Each developer may point this at their own UE install without touching the repo.
.ue-root

# Python bytecode — the editor's Python (Scripts/generate_map.py) drops these
# next to the source when a module is imported.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS noise
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.AppleDouble
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
Network Trash Folder
Temporary Items
Icon

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows noise
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linux noise
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*~
.directory
.Trash-*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Imported engine art — NOT ours, NOT committed.
#
# Scripts/import-mannequin.sh copies Epic's Mannequin (skeletal meshes, skeleton,
# animations, ABP_Unarmed, materials, textures — ~126 MB) out of each developer's
# own UE 5.8 install into Content/Characters/Mannequins, where the assets' own
# embedded /Game references require them to be.
#
# Everyone is pinned to the same engine version, so everyone gets byte-identical
# files. Importing them beats committing them: ~126 MB of art nobody has to pay
# LFS bandwidth for on every clone, and nothing here is content we authored or may
# redistribute. (The repo is NOT "text-only" any more — spec v17 committed the
# baked arena, the materials, the input, character and UI assets. That claim used
# to be here and it was retired with the rest of build contract 2.)
#
# Run Scripts/import-mannequin.sh after cloning. Without it the game still runs —
# ATraceCharacter falls back to a team-coloured capsule and logs a warning.
#
# Scoped to the imported folder only, and anchored to the repo root, so the rest
# of Content/ (notably /Content/Maps/Arena.umap, which IS ours and IS tracked)
# is untouched.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Content/Characters/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer scratch space inside Content/ — spec v17 §1.
#
# Content/Developers/<you>/ is Unreal's OWN convention for personal work-in-progress
# assets: the Content Browser has a "Show Developers Content" toggle and drops new
# assets there. Both directories exist on this machine already and were NOT ignored,
# so the first person to save a test asset would have pushed it into the team's LFS
# storage without meaning to — and LFS storage counts EVERY version FOREVER, so that
# is not recoverable without rewriting history.
#
# Content/Collections/ is the editor's saved-search files. They are per-person
# working state, they churn constantly, and nobody has ever needed one of someone
# else's. If your team later decides a shared collection is worth versioning,
# delete the second line rather than adding a "!" exception (git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded).
#
# Both anchored to the repo root so they cannot accidentally match anything else.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Content/Developers/
/Content/Collections/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly kept (belt-and-braces, and documentation for the next person).
# These are anchored to the repo root and re-include nothing that is ignored
# above — they exist so a careless future edit is obvious in review.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/Config/
!/Source/
!/Scripts/
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore

# Generated art (Scripts/generate_content.py). Binary, regenerated per developer
# from the pinned UE 5.8.1 install - never committed. See the asset policy in
# Scripts/generate_content.py.
/Content/Generated/

# Licensed fonts: usable per-developer, NEVER redistributed. This repo is public.
# See Scripts/generate_font_atlas.py and docs/FONTS.md.
Art/Fonts/*.otf
Art/Fonts/*.ttf
Art/Fonts/*.pdf

# ...EXCEPT the open-licence ones, which are the whole point of having an interim face.
# Lato is SIL Open Font Licence 1.1: redistribution IS permitted (and required to carry the
# licence, which Art/Fonts/README.md does). Spec v20 §1 asks for the interim .ttf to be
# committed so a clean clone can re-run the import; the blanket rules above were written for
# Sofachrome, which is commercial and must stay out. Keep this list to fonts whose licence you
# have actually read - never add MyriadPro, ProximaNova, TrajanPro or Sofachrome.
!Art/Fonts/Lato-Regular.ttf
# Lato is SIL OFL — safe to commit, unlike the licensed faces above.
!Art/Fonts/Lato-Regular.ttf
!Art/Fonts/README*

# *** THE SAME LICENCE RULE, AT THE REPO ROOT. Spec v25 integration pass. ***
# The rules above only ever matched Art/Fonts/. Working copies of the licensed faces and the
# archives they arrive in have repeatedly been dropped at the repo ROOT instead — at the time this
# was written that was Erbaum-Bold.otf, sofachrome.zip and "font files test.zip", all untracked,
# none ignored. The house rule is that everything is staged with `git add -A`, and this repo is
# PUBLIC, so the next commit would have redistributed commercially-licensed type.
#
# Root only (the leading slash): Content/ and Art/ keep their own explicit rules above, and a
# blanket *.otf would silently swallow a font somebody deliberately vendored elsewhere.
/*.otf
/*.ttf
/*.zip

# Git LFS re-installs its own hooks into whatever core.hooksPath points at (see
# Scripts/setup-hooks.sh). Those four are generated per machine and per git-lfs
# version, so the repo ships only the hook we wrote and lets LFS lay its own.
.githooks/post-checkout
.githooks/post-commit
.githooks/post-merge
.githooks/pre-push
